   "text": {
    "L1": "To multiply a two-digit number, split it into tens and ones.",
    "L2": "For 47 times 6, split 47 into 40 and 7.",
    "L3": "Multiply both parts: 40 times 6 is 240, and 7 times 6 is 42.",
    "L4": "Now add the two products: 240 plus 42 equals 282.",
    "L5": "An estimate checks the answer: 47 times 6 is near 40 times 6, or 240.",
    "L6": "Multiplying only the ones is a mistake. The tens must be multiplied too.",
    "L7": "Multiplying by 10 moves every digit one place to the left. So 23 times 10 is 230.",
    "L8": "Now choose the correct answer for 23 times 4."
   },
